<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 5.8 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 5.8 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 5.8 percent in the week of December 11 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 6.5 percent.(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			   Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  21.60	  21.39	     20.42</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	1.95	   1.99		1.76</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
